  "description": "The medical humanities minor is tailored to students pursuing careers in healthcare, medical research, or public health who also wish to explore the insights offered by fields such as English, history, communication, political science, philosophy, and religion. Calvin's medical humanities program is housed in the Department of Philosophy, which provides a foundation in ethics. Building on this foundation, students will complete courses across four distribution domains. The minor invites students to reflect on their health-related careers through fundamental questions: What does it look like to love my neighbor as myself? What makes a just society? What does it mean to be human? What is it to live well?",
